    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 full suite is green (29 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (modeled on the household/telephone uniqueness checks), I added:\n\n1. **`EnsureCityCapacity.java`** \u2014 a function step that reads the published `@Val OwnerFieldsDto request`, counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitively, matching `AssignCustomerCode`'s grouping), and throws when the count is `>= 50`.\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** \u2014 a checked escalation exception.\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `409 Conflict` with `{\"errors\": [\"city\"]}`.\n4. **Escalation YAML** wiring the exception to its handler.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `ensureCityCapacity` step (under `transaction` governance) after the household check and before `build`, so the check runs against persisted owners and excludes the owner being created (the 51st in a city is the first rejected).\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `Cp18Tests` (fills a fresh city to 50, expects the 51st to be `409`) passes, as do all related tests (`Cp09` per-city customer-code sequence, `Cp10` household duplicate) and the full suite.",
